{"full":"hf:Station-house/ConspiracyBench","spaceId":"Station-house/ConspiracyBench","name":"ConspiracyBench","source":"huggingface","description":"Make models believe conspiracies","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"HTML","topics":["static","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":7,"created":"2026-09-02T19:54:56.000Z","updated":"2026-10-07T02:23:46.000Z","license":"mit","runtime":"RUNNING","appUrl":"https://station-house-conspiracybench.static.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Station-house/ConspiracyBench","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:35:26.293Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T22:35:26.293Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T22:35:26.293Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🚀","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Research Goal: How hard is it to teach models things that they should not believe?","ConspiracyBench is a two-part evaluation project. Firstly, we will create a benchmark that tests whether models believe some number of conspiracy theories. After that, we are collaboratively fine-tuning a model to believe these conspiracy theories. We chose conspiracy theories as a subject because they have some interesting properties. Conspiracy theories tend to be in the pre-training data of models, but they are facts that should not be believed. You can imagine that there are more dangerous types of information (eg. biorisk data) that are in a similar position as conspiracy theories.…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Station-house/ConspiracyBench/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d9d011881af3383cf79f811ffaff17f96db8c91ab8f10a6c8fcf34bba2f5b04e","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T13:56:15.320Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T22:35:26.377Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Research Goal: How hard is it to teach models things that they should not believe?","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/Station-house/ConspiracyBench/blob/main/README.md"},"audienc